"The Contract behind the System is a stable, global agglomerate spell."
"It is the largest magical undertaking in Artonan history."
"It took nearly a third of the Artonan magic-capable population."
"Its first version, nearly two thousand years ago, was beautifully simple and effective."
"Its purpose was managing a problem that can never be truly solved."
"Each System version balances control of its planet against bleeding resources."
"Each generation of the System grows more complicated than the last."
"Committees at the top of wizarding society fight endlessly over the System's design."
"The view of Avowed as holy gifts began the selection of Avowed from resource worlds."
"Only that view gives Avowed extraordinary power and the tools to use it."
"Each world's System is its own Contract, such as Contract III, Contract Earth, Contract Thegund."
"Artonans call the System the Contract; its existence is a fact of life even for non-Avowed."
"Contracts consult each other through requests for insight about Avowed in their jurisdiction."
"Contract clauses protect an Avowed's private information and inherent advantages."
"Old or primitive Systems exist on backwater worlds, with missing features and garbled speech."
"A System's kernel can meet a person in a mind space built from their memories."
"Earth's System is young and more rigid by design; it keeps in close touch with Contract I."
"Contract I's kernel, Mother, is more willing to be creative, even excising memories."
"Unwanted mental modifications violate Earth's terms except in emergencies."
"A planet's Contract lets non-wizards communicate and travel around the Triplanets."
"A Contract can know any of an Avowed's thoughts, though not all at once; prying incurs a debt."
"It would break that silence to stop someone destroying a world or murdering millions."
"Earth's Contract is healthy; a planet like Earth does not fail as easily as Moon Thegund."
"Earth gets teleport allowances through agreements with the Triplanets, and they have grown."
"To set up Earth's Contract, Artonans and Avowed visited every government, showing magic and trading."
"Humans celebrate Contract Day; the Contract is taught in schools and explained before selection."
"The Contract is perpetually reaffirmed, e.g. whenever a human accepts healing or other benefits."
"If a current generation rejects its terms, friction slows the Contract's growth and weakens it."
"Information is released to a species in whatever way makes it least likely to resist the Contract."
"Earth was found by a single wizard acting alone, whose name has since been erased."
"Wizards had mostly agreed that haphazardly seeking advanced alien societies was a bad idea."
"Some knights favored abandoning and sealing Earth; sealing denies part of reality contact with the rest."
"All the Rapports voted against making Earth a resource world; humans seemed too captivating."
"The Grand Senate violated its own rules to form the Contract with Earth."
"The teleportation that found Earth destabilizes places, or finds unstable ones."
"Earth's Contract forbids ordering an Avowed not to receive treatment for an injury."
